{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.sum_of_positive_qInteger_products_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.sum_of_positive_qInteger_products_pos","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/HeckeEnergyPositivity.lean#L124-L136","doc":"Sums of products of rescaled q-integers (with positive factors)\nare positive. This is the abstract structural fact behind the\nHecke-trace functional summing positive Wedderburn weights. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.positive_ratio_of_positive_qIntegers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.positive_ratio_of_positive_qIntegers","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/HeckeEnergyPositivity.lean#L105-L120","doc":"**Hecke-energy cost is non-negative when q > 0.** This is the\nabstract statement: any cost expressible as a finite product of\nrescaled q-integer ratios (i.e. a Wedderburn weight\n`w_λ(q) = dim_q(V_λ)^2 / [n]_q!`) inherits positivity from\n`qIntegerRescaled_pos`.\n\nThe actual hook-length-formula content requires Young diagrams,\ndeferred to `MathlibBridge.lean`. Here we record the abstract\nstructural fact: ratios of positive q-integers are positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled_strict_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled_strict_mono","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/HeckeEnergyPositivity.lean#L93-L101","doc":"**Strict monotonicity of the rescaled q-integer at `q > 1`.**\nFor `q > 1`, the rescaled q-integer grows with `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled_pos","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/HeckeEnergyPositivity.lean#L75-L91","doc":"**Positivity of the rescaled q-integer at `q > 0`.** For every\n`q > 0` and `k ≥ 1`, the rescaled q-integer is strictly positive.\n\nProof: `qIntegerRescaled q k = ∑_{j=0}^{k-1} q^{2j}` is a sum\nof `k ≥ 1` terms, each positive (since `q^{2j} > 0` when\n`q > 0`). Sum of positive terms is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled_succ","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/HeckeEnergyPositivity.lean#L67-L71","doc":"Recurrence: `qIntegerRescaled q (k+1) = qIntegerRescaled q k + q^{2k}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled_one","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/HeckeEnergyPositivity.lean#L63-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled_zero","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/HeckeEnergyPositivity.lean#L59-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/HeckeEnergyPositivity.lean#L44-L57","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical geometric bracket.**\n\n`QIntegerCanonical` names this definition as *the* live example of legitimate\ngeometric usage — \"correct only where the variable means `q²`\".  This turns that\ndocumented claim into a theorem: the rescaled bracket is literally `qIntGeo`\nevaluated at `q²`, unconditionally.\n\nConsolidating it onto `qIntBal` would have been the mis-migration the module\nwarns about; consolidating it onto `qIntGeo (q ^ 2)` is the *correct* one, and\nhaving it as an equation means the site is no longer an unexplained straggler in\nthe census. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HeckeEnergyPositivity.qIntegerRescaled","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/HeckeEnergyPositivity.lean#L33-L42","doc":"The *rescaled* q-integer\n\n`qIntegerRescaled q k = ∑_{j=0}^{k-1} q^{2j}`\n\nThis is `[k]_q · q^{k-1}` where `[k]_q = (q^k - q^{-k}) /\n(q - q^{-1})` is the standard q-integer. The rescaled form\navoids negative exponents and lives entirely in `ℕ`-powers,\nmaking positivity proofs trivial. ","signatureChunk":0}]}